      "greedy_continuation": " what is the use of a book,\" thought Alice, \"without pictures or conversations?\" So she was considering whether she had not better go and ask what she could do to amuse herself, when she saw a little white object moving rapidly down the stream, and coming towards her.\n\nIt was",
      "samples": [
        " is not at all entertaining,\" she said to herself.\n\n\"Well, I'm getting too old for this.\" And Alice began to move restlessly about again. \"I believe it's too warm to be comfortable here,\" she said; \"let's try a draught.\"\n\nSo",
        " is as dull as dish-water.\"\n\n\"Are you not well, Alice?\" said her sister.\n\n\"No, I am not well, indeed, Catterina; I am very ill indeed,\" replied Alice, \"and am quite ashamed of myself for being ill, and don",
        " what is the use of a book to a person who can't read?\" So, now, being very lonely, she took out her pocket-handkerchief, and pulling a long stem of grass, began to pass it through her teeth, in order to chew the end; and here she was"
      ],
