      "greedy_continuation": " lay before me. I had been a long time in the work, and I was weary. I had been a long time in the work, and I was weary. I had been a long time in the work, and I was weary. I had been a long time in the work, and",
      "samples": [
        " lay before me. I gathered up the broken fragments of its shattered frame with an anxious hand, and gazed into the dilated eyes, which burned with an unnatural light, and fixed an vacant, investigatory expression upon my own. I gazed long and earnestly, for I thought that in that look I",
        " lay in the coffin, and I watched for the first gasp of animation. But it never came.\n\nAfter a long useless struggle, I was compelled to give it up, in despair. My mother was then at her wit's end as to what to do with it. She vowed that",
        " I held in my hand.\n\nV\n\nIn the month of March, during the season of February, in the town of the city of Boston, I was favoured by the presence of a gentleman, whom I shall call Mr. Thomas Bailey, a gentleman of ability, truth, and honour"
      ],
