      "greedy_continuation": " Adler, but he was always conscious of a certain fascination and power in her presence. He was never able to analyse the reason of this, but he was sure that it was not the mere fascination of her beauty. It was something deeper, something more subtle, something more complex. He was never",
      "samples": [
        " Adler, but simply that he felt no emotion whatever, except the one he called 'the interest of the case', and that was the sole reason why he concentrated all his thoughts upon little Miss Irene Adler when he sat alone in his rooms at 221B Baker Street.'\n\n'She has",
        " Adler, but that he was always conscious of the dominance and the climax of her personality, so that no other woman could ever come up to his idea of her ideal.\n\nI wonder if I can ever win his love. He gave the impression of being immune to all the female charms",
        " Adler; but, indeed, he could not feel any emotion at all. He accepted her with a sort of contemptuous tolerance. To him she was a woman, and that was all.\n\nYet he had a certain weakness for her. He had a longing to touch and handle her."
      ],
