      "greedy_continuation": ", where the enemy was driven back, and the enemy's machine-guns were silenced.\n\nThe enemy's artillery was now very active, and the enemy's infantry were seen to be advancing in great numbers. The enemy's artillery was also very active, and the enemy's infantry were seen to",
      "samples": [
        " batteries, the latter of which were ordered to retire when they had sustained too many casualties; and in this attack also five guns were knocked out.\n\nWe were now so weak in the batteries that our front was held by two companies only; yet, although a good deal of effort was made to",
        ", in the vicinity of the railway embankment. The enemy made numerous attempts to pass from one trench to the other, some of these by means of a deep-dug tunnel, and others by scaling the walls of the trench. But they were always driven back, and were finally driven out",
        ". We were under a hurricane of fire. Parallel with the fire from the enemy, the whole of No. 14 was shooting at us. It was a very difficult thing to starve the Germans; if they got food we got it, but if they could get ammunition we could not get it"
      ],
