      "greedy_continuation": " If you are working in the round, work the dec row as follows: Dec 4 sts in each cable (to dec: work 2 tog across each cable). In next row complete 8th pattern row. NEXT ROW: K 2 at each end, K 2 tog across remainder",
      "samples": [
        " Stitch the decs as worked.\n\n#    \n_Joan of Arc_\n\nJoan of Arc was a Frenchwoman who later became the leader of the French revolt against the English. When the English defeated the French at the battle of Orléans in 1429 she was",
        " Cast-on and bind off are confusing if you have not previously worked the cable pattern, so refer to the cable chart below for the cable pattern.\n\nDOUBLE-INTERLOCK CROCHET\n\nCast-on, bind off:  dc in 2nd chain from hook, dc",
        " 2 rows dec will make short socks. Fleece yarn for Knit Socks Patterned on a 4-Row Garter Stitch Cable Pattern. NOTE: This pattern is for knitted socks. Fleece yarn is not recommended. Pattern is written to Knit Socks on a 4"
      ],
