      "greedy_continuation": " was a great splash and a yell of \"Yankee Doodle!\"\n\n\"What's the matter?\" asked the boatman, as he came up.\n\n\"I'm a-going to drown!\" said Ephraim, \"and I don't care!\"\n\n",
      "samples": [
        " was a desperate match: the boatman headed for shore and the Yankee boy sprang to the boat, grasped the second oar and kept them both from the shore. As nothing could be done, the boatman resumed his charge, and Ephraim in his turn was brought within the reach of",
        " was a terrific scrimmage.\n\n\"Hold your dang' head, ye black pirutty!\" roared Ephraim, when he recovered himself. The boatman got up and received a hearty <DW8> in the face from the gallant boy. \"G'wan,",
        " was a whirlpool, but which presently settled down as quiet as a millpond.\" \"What if that had been a French boat?\" exclaimed Zebulon, as he assisted the boatman out of the water and got him on his feet. \"You think now you have got me,\""
      ],
