      "greedy_continuation": " as it is liable to stick to the paper.\n\n_To make a BREAD PUDDING._—Take a pound of flour, a pound of butter, a pound of sugar, a pound of currants, a pound of raisins, a pound of currants, a",
      "samples": [
        " but it should be carefully cut, and not comminuted. Place in a pan, and place in the oven when it is in the oven, so that it may be used while it is being toasted.—Then take the white of a young egg, and mix it with cold water, and put",
        " as it is always soiled when the paper is slightly moistened.\n\nIt is, however, for the purpose of photographing bread very much that we use the home-made, or the kind that comes to us in large quantities. It is absolutely indispensable that it should be perfectly fresh—",
        " as bread should be eaten on a clean; and if it has dried butter, the butter is to be burnt off and rubbed clean before the bread is broken. When concluded, the portion of the bread on the bottom should be trodden from on top, to render the milk run out more quickly,"
