      "greedy_continuation": " roots.\n\nThe plant's roots are the part of the plant that absorbs water and minerals from the soil.\n\nThe plant's leaves are the part of the plant that absorbs water and minerals from the air.\n\nThe plant's leaves are the part of the plant that absor",
      "samples": [
        " roots, which are located in its centre. The leaves and air are consumed on the way.\n\nWhat happens to the water that is taken up is that, after the process of absorption, it mixes with the minerals in the plant and circulates through the plant. If the plant is young,",
        " roots. They are carried through pores in the plant and make up the plant's _vascular tissues_ (the inner bark, wood, and leaves). The water and minerals are then taken up by the _xylem_ (the _transpiration stream_ ) and the _phloem_",
        " roots.\nFrom the soil, water, minerals and chemicals are moved through the plant’s vascular system and transported throughout the plant body to its various parts.\nThe vascular system is a twining network of tubes and vessels.\nEach plant cell is surrounded by a cell wall.\n\nA"
      ],
