      "greedy_continuation": " its _circumference ratio_.\n\nThe ratio of the circumference of a circle to its diameter is called its _circumference ratio_.\n\nThe ratio of the circumference of a circle to its diameter is called its _circumference ratio_.\n\nThe ratio of the circumference of a circle to its",
      "samples": [
        " its _circumference_ and the ratio of its diameter to its diameter is called its _circumference_ again.\n\nA parabola's vertex is the point at which it is tangent to each of its two lines.\n\nThe ratio of an arc's length to its diameter is called",
        " its _circumference to diameter ratio_ , or _C/D ratio._\n\nThe circumference can be calculated using the formula 3π _R_ , where _R_ is the _radius_ of the circle. The diameter is also the _radius._\n\nThe _circumference of",
        " its _circumference;_ the diameter is called its _radius._ In the figure, if the radius of the circle is 8 inches, its circumference is 16 inches. If the radius is 9 inches, the circumference is 15 inches.\n\n...while the diameter of a circle is the distance around"
