      "greedy_continuation": " thermometer. The thermometer is a glass tube with a bulb at one end and a metal rod at the other. The bulb is heated to a high temperature and the metal rod is placed in the air. The bulb is then cooled to a low temperature and the metal rod is read. The temperature",
      "samples": [
        " thermometer, which is a bulb filled with a liquid, the air temperature, and marked with degrees Fahrenheit. A different instrument, the barometer, is used to record the height of the atmosphere. A barometer is marked with inches of mercury. One inch of mercury is equal to 32",
        " thermometer, a device that measures the temperature of air over a wide area. An average temperature is the average of the temperatures measured. A temperature is also an average of the temperatures measured at a (usually small) number of places.\n\nAviation has been part of the fabric of human life",
        " thermometer. It is not a good measure of air pressure, which is why you should always turn off your air conditioning when you leave your home. Unless you live in a very warm climate, the actual temperature of the air in your house is about the same as the temperature of the air outside."
      ],
