      "samples": [
        " called Zeus (Greek: Ζεύς)\nThe origins of the name Zeus derives from the name of the Greek god Jupiter, who was one of the gods of the Roman pantheon.\nThe name Zeus is derived from Zēos (Greek: Ζε",
        " Cronos, the ruler of the universe and father of the gods Zeus, Hades, Poseidon, Hestia, Demeter, Hera, Aphrodite, Hestia, Persephone, and Iris. Cronos was said to have \"wrapped",
