      "greedy_continuation": " Milky Way.\n\nThe Sun is the largest and most massive star in the Milky Way.\n\nThe Sun is a red giant star.\n\nThe Sun is a yellow dwarf star.\n\nThe Sun is a white dwarf star.\n\nThe Sun is a red giant star.\n",
      "samples": [
        " Milky Way. The Sun is located at the center of the Milky Way. Other stars, planets, and other objects orbit the Sun. The Solar System has an orbital radius of about 150,000 miles from the center of the Milky Way.\n\nThe Moon orbits the Earth, and the Earth orbits",
        " Milky Way.\n\nIn galactic terms, the Milky Way is the size of the full moon. The galaxy is about 100,000 light years in diameter, and contains billions of stars.\n\nThe size of the milky way is larger than the sun, but is smaller than the galaxy U",
        " Milky Way. The Sun is in a relatively young part of the Galaxy (see our Universe Map). The Earth is the third-largest planet in the Solar System after Jupiter and Saturn. The Sun was created 10,000,000,000,000,000,000,000 years ago, and"
      ],
