      "greedy_continuation": " string family.\n\nThe violin, viola and cello are all made of wood.\n\nThe violin, viola and cello are all made of wood.\n\nThe violin, viola and cello are all made of wood.\n\nThe violin, viola and cell",
      "samples": [
        " string family. String instruments are also known as ‘strings’.\n\nViolins, violas, cellos and double basses typically have four, five, six and seven strings respectively.\n\nThe original name of the violin was the ‘viola da gamba’.\n\nThe cell",
        " strings. Violins are played by the left hand and are sometimes also called bass viols, and violas are played with the right hand and are sometimes also called tenors. Cellos are played with both hands and are sometimes called double basses.\n\nThe melody comes from the end of",
        " stringed instruments. The violin and viola are both plucked instruments, whereas the cello is an instrument with a reed instead of a pick.\n\nDifferent people have different techniques for playing, but they all play a similar sound.\n\nThe most important part of a piece is the"
